The initial search failed to retrieve records, and the PubMed query was too restrictive; the guideline page also blocked access. The clinical question is nevertheless specific: a sibling is a first-degree relative with onset in adolescence, so ongoing family surveillance—not a one-time or symptom-triggered test—is the key issue. I’ll make one focused follow-up search for the screening interval and recommended modalities.

