The standard recommendation for an at-risk child is serial clinical screening with ECG and echocardiography, with shorter intervals when family disease presented early; genetic testing depends on identifying a pathogenic variant in the affected relative. Of the listed options, annual echocardiography is the closest, although it omits the accompanying ECG and represents the intensive end of the usual interval. I’ll check one more targeted guideline source before finalizing.

